{"id":8817,"date":"2024-06-21T07:00:00","date_gmt":"2024-06-21T07:00:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/?p=8817"},"modified":"2026-05-27T09:56:40","modified_gmt":"2026-05-27T09:56:40","slug":"what-you-need-to-know-about-permitting","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/what-you-need-to-know-about-permitting\/","title":{"rendered":"What You Need To Know About Permitting"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Embarking on a <a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/services\/\">new construction project<\/a> or renovation endeavor is an exciting venture, but navigating the intricate world of permitting can be a daunting task, especially for those unfamiliar with the process. Securing the necessary permits from local authorities is essential to ensure that your project meets safety regulations and adheres to zoning ordinances. In this comprehensive guide, we&#8217;ll demystify the permitting process, shedding light on the intricacies of obtaining building permits, the various types available, associated costs, and the timeline for approval. Whether you find yourself in Portland, OR, Tigard, OR, or any other locale, understanding the nuances of permitting is crucial for a successful project. And remember, if the intricacies of permitting seem overwhelming, don&#8217;t hesitate to seek assistance from seasoned professionals like <a title=\"\" href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/\">Harris &amp; Sons<\/a>, who can guide you through the process with expertise and efficiency.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/two-professional-engineers-creating-a-new-building-2023-11-27-05-05-12-utc-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"new construction project\" class=\"wp-image-8820\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What Is a Building Permit?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A building permit is an official document issued by local authorities that grants you permission to begin construction on a new home or remodel an existing structure. This permit ensures your project adheres to local building codes and safety regulations. Essentially, it authorizes the builder to construct or modify the building legally. Understanding construction permit requirements is essential to avoid any legal or safety issues during your project.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What Are the Different Types of Permits Available?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">There are primarily two types of permits: residential and nonresidential.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Residential Permits:<\/strong> These are typically required for new homes, additions, or significant alterations to existing homes. If you&#8217;re planning a home renovation in Beaverton, OR, or Hillsboro, OR, you&#8217;ll need to secure a residential permit. <\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Nonresidential Permits:<\/strong> These cover commercial buildings, schools, churches, and other non-residential structures. If you&#8217;re building or renovating an office complex in Lake Oswego, OR, a nonresidential permit is necessary.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What Does a Permit Cost?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The cost of obtaining a permit varies based on several factors, including the project&#8217;s size, whether it&#8217;s new construction or an addition, and the location. For instance, permit fees in Hillsboro, OR, may differ from those in Prineville, OR. Generally, larger and more complex projects incur higher permit costs.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Permit Fee Breakdown<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here&#8217;s a general permit pricing guide to give you an idea:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Small Projects (e.g., minor remodels):<\/strong> $100 &#8211; $500<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Medium Projects (e.g., room additions):<\/strong> $500 &#8211; $2,000<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Large Projects (e.g., new home construction):<\/strong> $2,000 and up<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To get an accurate estimate, contact your local building department. They can provide specific details about construction permit fees and any additional costs you might incur.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How Long Does It Take to Obtain a Permit?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The permit application process can take anywhere from a few days to several months, depending on the project&#8217;s complexity and the efficiency of the local building department. In areas like Bend, OR, and Redmond, OR, the processing time might differ.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here are some factors that influence the permit approval duration:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Project Size and Complexity:<\/strong> Larger projects often require more detailed plans and reviews, extending the approval timeframe.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Local Regulations:<\/strong> Different cities and counties have varying regulations that can affect the speed of the process.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Department Workload:<\/strong> During peak construction seasons, the local building department might experience delays due to high application volumes.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/businessman-on-cell-phone-in-building-under-constr-2023-11-27-05-21-44-utc-1024x684.jpg\" alt=\"A man talking on the phone\" class=\"wp-image-8822\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Speeding Up the Permit Process<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To expedite the building permit timeline, consider the following tips:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Submit Complete Plans:<\/strong> Ensure your application includes all necessary documents and detailed plans to avoid delays caused by incomplete submissions.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Follow Up Regularly:<\/strong> Stay in contact with the building department to track the progress of your application.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Hire a Professional:<\/strong> Experienced contractors can navigate the permitting process more efficiently and handle any issues that arise.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What Are the Requirements for a Building Permit? (And Why Do They Matter?)<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Different types of building permits have specific requirements and restrictions. Understanding these is crucial for compliance and safety. For instance:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Residential Permits:<\/strong> Typically cover single-family dwellings. Requirements often include architectural plans, site plans, and adherence to local zoning laws.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Commercial Permits:<\/strong> Issued for larger buildings like shopping centers and office complexes. These permits often require detailed engineering reports, fire safety plans, and environmental assessments.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The importance of building permits cannot be overstated. They ensure that all construction adheres to safety standards, protecting both the property owner and the public. Failing to obtain the necessary permits can result in fines, legal issues, and potential hazards.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What Happens If You Don&#8217;t Obtain a Permit?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Neglecting to obtain the required permits for your project can lead to several complications. Unpermitted work is often discovered during a home inspection, which can occur if you decide to sell your property. This can result in the need to reverse or redo work to comply with local regulations, incurring additional costs and delays. In some cases, fines and legal action may be taken against the property owner for non-compliance.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Moreover, unpermitted work can pose safety risks. Permits ensure that the construction adheres to building codes designed to safeguard the structure\u2019s integrity and occupants&#8217; safety. Without these checks, the work may not meet these critical standards, leading to potential hazards like structural failures, electrical fires, or plumbing issues.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Understanding Zoning Laws and Regulations<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Building permits also ensure compliance with local zoning laws, which dictate how properties in specific areas can be used. Zoning laws cover aspects like the type of buildings allowed, the density of buildings, and the nature of property use (residential, commercial, industrial, etc.). For instance, if you&#8217;re planning to build a detached garage in Clackamas, OR, or add an accessory dwelling unit (ADU) in Tigard, OR, understanding the zoning laws will help you determine what is permissible on your property.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Zoning laws can affect various aspects of your project, including the height of your structure, how far it must be set back from the street or neighboring properties, and even the aesthetic characteristics of the building. Failing to adhere to these regulations can result in the need to modify or demolish non-compliant structures, which can be both costly and time-consuming.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/legal-expert-in-the-digital-age-business-finance-2023-11-27-05-04-02-utc-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"A man working on the laptop\" class=\"wp-image-8824\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Leveraging Professional Assistance<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Navigating the intricacies of the permitting process can be overwhelming, especially for larger projects. Hiring a professional with experience in local regulations can be invaluable. A knowledgeable contractor can guide you through the permitting process, ensuring that all necessary permits are obtained and that your project complies with all relevant codes and regulations. This is particularly beneficial in areas with stringent rules, like <a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/best-construction-services-in-lake-oswego\/\">Lake Oswego, OR<\/a>, or Hillsboro, OR.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Professionals can also assist in preparing and submitting detailed plans and documents required for permit applications. Their expertise can help streamline the process, potentially reducing the time required for approval and minimizing the risk of errors that could delay your project.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Conclusion<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In conclusion, navigating the complexities of the permitting process is integral to the success of any construction or renovation endeavor. Building permits not only guarantee adherence to local regulations but also safeguard the structural integrity and safety of your property. Whether you&#8217;re embarking on a new construction project in Portland, OR, or planning a remodel in Beaverton, OR, securing the necessary permits is a non-negotiable step.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">By proactively planning, budgeting effectively, and enlisting professional assistance, you can streamline the permitting process and ensure compliance with regulatory requirements. Remember, with the support of seasoned professionals like <a href=\"https:\/\/share.google\/gwM2ovux57i85a4fn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Harris &amp; Son<\/a>s, obtaining permits and bringing your vision to life can be a seamless and stress-free experience. Don&#8217;t hesitate to leverage expert guidance to navigate the permitting journey and realize your dream project with confidence.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Embarking on a new construction project or renovation endeavor is an exciting venture, but navigating the intricate world of permitting can be a daunting task, especially for those unfamiliar with the process. Securing the necessary permits from local authorities is essential to ensure that your project meets safety regulations and adheres to zoning ordinances. In [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":8819,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[33,34,35,30,31,32],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-8817","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-remodeling-tips","category-addition-resources","category-basement-resources","category-bathroom-resources","category-contractors-guides","category-kitchen-resources"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/8817","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=8817"}],"version-history":[{"count":4,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/8817\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":16326,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/8817\/revisions\/16326"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=8817"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=8817"},{"ta